May you explain what's going on in this snippet of code? I am not familiar with it.

.action-panel{
    @apply fixed left-0 flex flex-col top-72 space-y-2;
}
.action-button{
  @apply bg-white relative top-2 py-2 text-center px-6;
}

reply:
# Explaining this CSS snippet

This is **CSS** using the **`@apply` directive**, which comes from **Tailwind CSS**. It lets you use Tailwind's utility classes inside a regular CSS rule, rather than writing them directly in your HTML.

## `.action-panel`

```css
.action-panel{
    @apply fixed left-0 flex flex-col top-72 space-y-2;
}
```

Translated to plain CSS, this roughly becomes:

```css
.action-panel {
    position: fixed;        /* fixed: stays in place when scrolling */
    left: 0;                /* pinned to the left edge of the viewport */
    display: flex;          /* flexbox layout */
    flex-direction: column; /* children stack vertically */
    top: 18rem;             /* top-72 → 18rem from the top (72 × 0.25rem) */
    /* space-y-2 → adds 0.5rem of gap between each direct child */
}
.action-panel > * + * {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
}
```

So `.action-panel` is a **fixed sidebar-like container pinned to the left side**, vertically stacked, starting 18rem from the top, with small gaps between its children.

## `.action-button`

```css
.action-button{
    @apply bg-white relative top-2 py-2 text-center px-6;
}
```

Plain CSS equivalent:

```css
.action-button {
    background-color: white;      /* bg-white */
    position: relative;           /* relative (enables top offset) */
    top: 0.5rem;                  /* top-2 → nudged down 0.5rem */
    padding-top: 0.5rem;          /* py-2 */
    padding-bottom: 0.5rem;       /* py-2 */
    text-align: center;           /* text-center */
    padding-left: 1.5rem;         /* px-6 */
    padding-right: 1.5rem;        /* px-6 */
}
```

So `.action-button` is a **white, centered, padded button** that is nudged down by a small amount relative to its normal position.

## Where this typically lives

In a Tailwind project, you'd put this in your main CSS file (e.g. `index.css` / `app.css`):

```css
@tailwind base;
@tailwind components;
@
